29781abc0c359f5b0b97eaf8e7de0924cb01ce92","file":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Rysers-Covering-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex","line":115,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"af6c1d9759f8d55417b8b59122ed7f73aaceef296a65b92845a488c609974d59","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Rysers-Covering-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9093d7e3febec391ea2bd80829781abc0c359f5b0b97eaf8e7de0924cb01ce92","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Rysers-Covering-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex#L115"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere exists $s_0$ such that, for every prime $s\\ge s_0$ with\n$s\\equiv2\\pmod3$, there is an integer $n_0(s)\\ge3$ with the following\nproperty. For every odd integer $n\\ge n_0(s)$, put $q=s^n$.\nThere is a finite intersecting $(q+1)$-partite $(q+1)$-uniform\nhypergraph $H$ satisfying\n\\[\n \\tau(H)=q+1.\n\\]\nIn particular, the intersecting case of~\\eqref{eq:ryser} is false."}
